# Tests for the Savers_credit module

Run with `clerk test`. Named scopes with the concrete cases of issue #29,
worked out by hand from Form 8880 (2024) and its instructions
(`sources/forms-instructions/f8880--2024.pdf`), IRC 25B and Notice 2023-75
(single 50 percent up to $23,000, 20 percent up to $25,000, 10 percent up to
$38,250; head of household $34,500, $37,500, $57,375; joint $46,000, $50,000,
$76,500). The oracle comparison is `make difftest SCOPE=savers_credit`.

> Using Types
> Using Savers_credit as S

## Helper: a return with defaults

By default: a single adult filer who is not a student and is not claimed as a
dependent, AGI $20,000, no spouse amounts, no distributions, and plenty of tax
(`total_tentative_tax` $10,000, no CDCC, no Schedule R credit). Each test
overrides what it needs.

```catala
declaration scope Case:
  context status content Types.FilingStatus
  context agi content money
  context p_deferrals content money
  context s_deferrals content money
  context p_dist content money
  context s_dist content money
  context p_under18 content boolean
  context p_student content boolean
  context p_claimed content boolean
  context s_under18 content boolean
  context s_student content boolean
  context s_claimed content boolean
  context mfj_dependent content boolean
  context tax content money
  context cdcc content money
  context edc content money
  context ko_three_years content boolean
  context ko_current content boolean
  context ko_contrib content boolean
  f scope S.SaversCredit
  output credit content money
  output line7 content money
  output line9 content decimal
  output line10 content money
  output line11 content money
  output qualified content boolean
  output unsupported content boolean

scope Case:
  definition status equals Types.FilingStatus.Single
  definition agi equals $20,000
  definition p_deferrals equals $0
  definition s_deferrals equals $0
  definition p_dist equals $0
  definition s_dist equals $0
  definition p_under18 equals false
  definition p_student equals false
  definition p_claimed equals false
  definition s_under18 equals false
  definition s_student equals false
  definition s_claimed equals false
  definition mfj_dependent equals false
  definition tax equals $10,000
  definition cdcc equals $0
  definition edc equals $0
  definition ko_three_years equals false
  definition ko_current equals false
  definition ko_contrib equals false

  definition f.filing_status equals status
  definition f.agi equals agi
  definition f.is_mfj_dependent equals mfj_dependent
  definition f.primary_filer_is_under18 equals p_under18
  definition f.primary_filer_is_student equals p_student
  definition f.primary_filer_is_claimed_as_dependent equals p_claimed
  definition f.secondary_filer_is_under18 equals s_under18
  definition f.secondary_filer_is_student equals s_student
  definition f.secondary_filer_is_claimed_as_dependent equals s_claimed
  definition f.primary_filer_total_deferrals_and_contributions equals p_deferrals
  definition f.secondary_filer_total_deferrals_and_contributions equals s_deferrals
  definition f.primary_filer_savers_gross_distributions equals p_dist
  definition f.secondary_filer_savers_gross_distributions equals s_dist
  definition f.total_tentative_tax equals tax
  definition f.cdcc_total_credit equals cdcc
  definition f.total_edc equals edc
  definition f.has_distributions_in_last_three_years equals ko_three_years
  definition f.has_current_year_distributions equals ko_current
  definition f.has_self_reported_contributions equals ko_contrib

  definition credit equals f.qualified_saver_credit_amount
  definition line7 equals f.combined_credit_limit
  definition line9 equals f.savers_credit_multiplier_as_rational
  definition line10 equals f.ratioed_combined_credit_limit
  definition line11 equals f.limitation_based_on_tax_liability
  definition qualified equals f.qualified_for_saver_credit
  definition unsupported equals f.unsupported
```

## Single, AGI $23,000, $2,000 deferred: 50 percent

AGI is at the top of the 50 percent band ("not over" $23,000). Line 6 is $2,000, line 9 is 0.5, line 10 is $1,000 (the maximum for a single filer).

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestSingle23000:
  c scope Case

scope TestSingle23000:
  definition c.agi equals $23,000
  definition c.p_deferrals equals $2,000
  assertion c.credit = $1,000
  assertion c.line7 = $2,000
  assertion c.line9 = 50%
  assertion c.line10 = $1,000
  assertion c.qualified
  assertion not c.unsupported
  # The spec rejects wrong outputs.
  assertion not (c.credit = $400)
  assertion not (c.credit = $2,000)
```

## Single, AGI $23,001: 20 percent

One dollar over the 50 percent bound: line 9 is 0.2 and the credit is $400.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestSingle23001:
  c scope Case

scope TestSingle23001:
  definition c.agi equals $23,001
  definition c.p_deferrals equals $2,000
  assertion c.credit = $400
  assertion c.line9 = 20%
  assertion not (c.credit = $1,000)
```

## Single, AGI $25,001: 10 percent

The 20 percent band ends at $25,000. $25,001 gives 0.1, so $200.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestSingle25001:
  c scope Case

scope TestSingle25001:
  definition c.agi equals $25,001
  definition c.p_deferrals equals $2,000
  assertion c.credit = $200
  assertion c.line9 = 10%
```

## Single, AGI $38,250: last dollar of the 10 percent band

Notice 2023-75 and Form 8880: single filers with AGI up to $38,250 get 10 percent.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestSingle38250:
  c scope Case

scope TestSingle38250:
  definition c.agi equals $38,250
  definition c.p_deferrals equals $2,000
  assertion c.credit = $200
  assertion c.line9 = 10%
```

## Single, AGI $38,251: no credit

Line 9 is zero: "If line 9 is zero, stop; you can't take this credit."

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestSingle38251:
  c scope Case

scope TestSingle38251:
  definition c.agi equals $38,251
  definition c.p_deferrals equals $2,000
  assertion c.credit = $0
  assertion c.line9 = 0%
  assertion not c.qualified
  assertion not (c.credit = $200)
```

## Married filing separately uses the single bands

Married filing separately and qualifying surviving spouse are in the "single" column of the line 9 table: AGI $24,000 gives 20 percent.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestMfs:
  c scope Case

scope TestMfs:
  definition c.status equals Types.FilingStatus.MarriedFilingSeparately
  definition c.agi equals $24,000
  definition c.p_deferrals equals $1,500
  assertion c.line9 = 20%
  assertion c.credit = $300
```

## Head of household bands

Head of household: 50 percent up to $34,500, 20 percent up to $37,500, 10 percent up to $57,375, zero above. AGI $37,000 with $1,000 deferred gives 0.2 times $1,000 = $200.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestHohBands:
  c scope Case

scope TestHohBands:
  definition c.status equals Types.FilingStatus.HeadOfHousehold
  definition c.agi equals $37,000
  definition c.p_deferrals equals $1,000
  assertion c.line9 = 20%
  assertion c.credit = $200
```

## Head of household, AGI $57,376: no credit

One dollar over the head of household limit.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestHoh57376:
  c scope Case

scope TestHoh57376:
  definition c.status equals Types.FilingStatus.HeadOfHousehold
  definition c.agi equals $57,376
  definition c.p_deferrals equals $2,000
  assertion c.credit = $0
```

## Married filing jointly, AGI $46,000, two filers

Each spouse deferred $2,000. Line 6 is $2,000 in each column, line 7 is $4,000, line 9 is 0.5, so the credit is $2,000 (the maximum for a joint return).

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestMfjTwoFilers46000:
  c scope Case

scope TestMfjTwoFilers46000:
  definition c.status equals Types.FilingStatus.MarriedFilingJointly
  definition c.agi equals $46,000
  definition c.p_deferrals equals $2,000
  definition c.s_deferrals equals $2,000
  assertion c.line7 = $4,000
  assertion c.line9 = 50%
  assertion c.line10 = $2,000
  assertion c.credit = $2,000
  assertion not (c.credit = $1,000)
```

## Married filing jointly, AGI $50,000: 20 percent

AGI $50,000 gives 0.2 on line 7 of $3,000 ($2,000 plus $1,000): $600.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestMfj50000:
  c scope Case

scope TestMfj50000:
  definition c.status equals Types.FilingStatus.MarriedFilingJointly
  definition c.agi equals $50,000
  definition c.p_deferrals equals $2,500
  definition c.s_deferrals equals $1,000
  assertion c.line7 = $3,000
  assertion c.credit = $600
```

## Married filing jointly, AGI $76,501: no credit

Joint limit is $76,500.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestMfj76501:
  c scope Case

scope TestMfj76501:
  definition c.status equals Types.FilingStatus.MarriedFilingJointly
  definition c.agi equals $76,501
  definition c.p_deferrals equals $2,000
  definition c.s_deferrals equals $2,000
  assertion c.credit = $0
```

## Deferrals above $2,000 count only up to $2,000

IRC 25B(a): "so much of the qualified retirement savings contributions ... as do not exceed $2,000". $5,000 deferred, line 6 is $2,000.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestDeferralsCapped:
  c scope Case

scope TestDeferralsCapped:
  definition c.agi equals $20,000
  definition c.p_deferrals equals $5,000
  assertion c.line7 = $2,000
  assertion c.credit = $1,000
```

## Contributions are reduced by distributions

Line 3 $2,000, line 4 $1,500, line 5 $500, credit 0.5 times $500 = $250.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestDistributionsReduce:
  c scope Case

scope TestDistributionsReduce:
  definition c.p_deferrals equals $2,000
  definition c.p_dist equals $1,500
  assertion c.line7 = $500
  assertion c.credit = $250
  assertion not (c.credit = $1,000)
```

## Distributions at or above contributions: no credit

Line 5 is not below zero: distributions $3,000 against $2,000 give $0 and line 7 is zero ("If zero, stop").

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestDistributionsExceed:
  c scope Case

scope TestDistributionsExceed:
  definition c.p_deferrals equals $2,000
  definition c.p_dist equals $3,000
  assertion c.line7 = $0
  assertion c.credit = $0
  assertion not c.qualified
```

## Joint return: both spouses' distributions in both columns

Form 8880 line 4: "If married filing jointly, include both spouses' amounts in both columns." The primary filer deferred $2,000 and the spouse $1,000; the spouse took a $500 distribution. Column (a) is $1,500, column (b) is $500; line 7 is $2,000; credit 0.5 times $2,000 = $1,000.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestMfjDistributionsBothColumns:
  c scope Case

scope TestMfjDistributionsBothColumns:
  definition c.status equals Types.FilingStatus.MarriedFilingJointly
  definition c.agi equals $40,000
  definition c.p_deferrals equals $2,000
  definition c.s_deferrals equals $1,000
  definition c.s_dist equals $500
  assertion c.line7 = $2,000
  assertion c.credit = $1,000
```

## DF-BUG(29-a): an ineligible spouse's distributions still reduce the contributions

The spouse is a full-time student (not an eligible individual) and took a $1,500 distribution; the primary filer deferred $2,000. IRC 25B(d)(2)(D) and the form instructions treat the spouse's distribution as received by the primary filer, so column (a) is $500 and the credit is 0.5 times $500 = $250. Direct File drops the ineligible spouse's distribution and gives $1,000.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestMfjIneligibleSpouseDistributions:
  c scope Case

scope TestMfjIneligibleSpouseDistributions:
  definition c.status equals Types.FilingStatus.MarriedFilingJointly
  definition c.agi equals $40,000
  definition c.p_deferrals equals $2,000
  definition c.s_student equals true
  definition c.s_dist equals $1,500
  assertion c.line7 = $500
  assertion c.credit = $250
  assertion not (c.credit = $1,000)
```

## Under 18: no credit

A filer who is under 18 (born after January 1, 2007) is not an eligible individual (IRC 25B(c)(1)).

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestUnder18:
  c scope Case

scope TestUnder18:
  definition c.p_under18 equals true
  definition c.p_deferrals equals $2,000
  assertion c.credit = $0
  assertion c.line7 = $0
  assertion not c.qualified
  assertion not (c.credit = $1,000)
```

## Student: no credit

IRC 25B(c)(2)(B): a student is not an eligible individual.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestStudent:
  c scope Case

scope TestStudent:
  definition c.p_student equals true
  definition c.p_deferrals equals $2,000
  assertion c.credit = $0
```

## Claimed as a dependent: no credit

IRC 25B(c)(2)(A).

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestClaimedAsDependent:
  c scope Case

scope TestClaimedAsDependent:
  definition c.p_claimed equals true
  definition c.p_deferrals equals $2,000
  assertion c.credit = $0
```

## Joint return, one spouse a student: only the other spouse's deferrals count

The student spouse's $2,000 does not count (line 2b is $0); the primary filer's $2,000 does. Credit 0.5 times $2,000 = $1,000.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestMfjOneSpouseStudent:
  c scope Case

scope TestMfjOneSpouseStudent:
  definition c.status equals Types.FilingStatus.MarriedFilingJointly
  definition c.agi equals $30,000
  definition c.p_deferrals equals $2,000
  definition c.s_deferrals equals $2,000
  definition c.s_student equals true
  assertion c.line7 = $2,000
  assertion c.credit = $1,000
```

## MFJ dependent: no credit

DF `/eligibleForSaversCredit` bans an MFJ dependent (a joint return filed only to claim a refund).

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestMfjDependent:
  c scope Case

scope TestMfjDependent:
  definition c.status equals Types.FilingStatus.MarriedFilingJointly
  definition c.mfj_dependent equals true
  definition c.p_deferrals equals $2,000
  assertion c.credit = $0
```

## Limited by tax liability

Credit Limit Worksheet: line 18 $1,000, less CDCC $300 and the credit for the elderly or disabled $200, leaves $500 for line 11. The tentative credit is $1,000, so line 12 is $500.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestLimitedByTax:
  c scope Case

scope TestLimitedByTax:
  definition c.agi equals $20,000
  definition c.p_deferrals equals $2,000
  definition c.tax equals $1,000
  definition c.cdcc equals $300
  definition c.edc equals $200
  assertion c.line10 = $1,000
  assertion c.line11 = $500
  assertion c.credit = $500
  assertion not (c.credit = $1,000)
```

## No tax left after CDCC: no credit

Line 11 is zero or less: "you can't take the credit".

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestNoTaxLeft:
  c scope Case

scope TestNoTaxLeft:
  definition c.p_deferrals equals $2,000
  definition c.tax equals $400
  definition c.cdcc equals $400
  assertion c.line11 = $0
  assertion c.credit = $0
  assertion not c.qualified
  assertion c.line10 = $1,000
```

## Line 10 rounds to whole dollars

A 10 percent credit on $5 of contributions is $0.50, rounded to $1 (ties away from zero).

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestRoundHalf:
  c scope Case

scope TestRoundHalf:
  definition c.agi equals $30,000
  definition c.p_deferrals equals $5
  assertion c.line10 = $1
```

## Self-reported distributions knock the return out

DF `/saversCreditKnockouts`: the filer qualifies and has distributions in the last three years.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestKnockout:
  c scope Case

scope TestKnockout:
  definition c.p_deferrals equals $2,000
  definition c.ko_three_years equals true
  assertion c.unsupported
```

## No knockout when the filer does not qualify

The knockout is conditioned on qualifying for the credit (AGI too high).

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestNoKnockoutWithoutCredit:
  c scope Case

scope TestNoKnockoutWithoutCredit:
  definition c.agi equals $90,000
  definition c.p_deferrals equals $2,000
  definition c.ko_current equals true
  assertion not c.unsupported
```
